inidad &amp; Tobago</option><option value="Tunisia">Tunisia</option><option value="Turkey">Turkey</option><option value="Turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</option><option value="Turks and Caicos Islands">Turks and Caicos Islands</option><option value="Tuvalu">Tuvalu</option><option value="Uganda">Uganda</option><option value="Ukraine">Ukraine</option><option value="United Arab Emirates">United Arab Emirates</option><option value="United Kingdom">United Kingdom</option><option value="Uruguay">Uruguay</option><option value="Uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</option><option value="Vanuatu">Vanuatu</option><option value="Holy See (Vatican City State)">Vatican City</option><option value="Venezuela, Bolivarian Republic of">Venezuela</option><option value="Viet Nam">Vietnam</option><option value="Virgin Islands, British">Virgin Islands, British</option><option value="Wallis and Futuna">Wallis and Futuna</option><option value="Western Sahara">Western Sahara</option><option value="Yemen">Yemen</option><option value="Zambia">Zambia</option><option value="Zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</option></select><span id="InstructCountry" tabindex="-1" class="mktoInstruction"></span><div class="mktoClear"></div></div><div class="mktoClear"></div></div><div class="mktoClear"></div></div><div class="mktoFormRow full-width"><div class="mktoFieldDescriptor mktoFormCol" style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><div class="mktoOffset" style="width: 10px;"></div><div class="mktoFieldWrap mktoRequiredField u-d-flex"><label for="Gated_Content_Opt_In__c" id="LblGated_Content_Opt_In__c" class="mktoLabel mktoHasWidth sr-only" style="width: 440.906px;"><div class="mktoAsterix">*</div>I acknowledge that submitting this form subscribes me to marketing communications regarding Webflow’s products, services, and events. I understand I can unsubscribe at any time.</label><div class="mktoGutter mktoHasWidth" style="width: 9.98438px;"></div><div title="I’d like to receive marketing communications regarding Webflow’s products, services, and events. I understand I can unsubscribe at any time." class="mktoLogicalField mktoCheckboxList mktoHasWidth mktoRequired" style="width: 19.5px;"><input name="Gated_Content_Opt_In__c" id="Gated_Content_Opt_In__c" type="checkbox" value="yes" aria-required="true" aria-labelledby="LblGated_Content_Opt_In__c InstructGated_Content_Opt_In__c" class="mktoField"><label for="Gated_Content_Opt_In__c" id="LblGated_Content_Opt_In__c"></label></div><span id="InstructGated_Content_Opt_In__c" tabindex="-1" class="mktoInstruction">I’d like to receive marketing communications regarding Webflow’s products, services, and events. I understand I can unsubscribe at any time.</span><div class="mktoClear"></div></div><div class="mktoClear"></div></div><div class="mktoClear"></div></div><div class="mktoButtonRow"><span class="mktoButtonWrap mktoSimple" style="margin-left: 120px;"><button type="submit" class="mktoButton">Subscribe</button></span></div><input type="hidden" name="formid" class="mktoField mktoFieldDescriptor" value="1591"><input type="hidden" name="munchkinId" class="mktoField mktoFieldDescriptor" value="050-LKC-745"></form></div></div><div data-form="success-wrapper" class="u-d-none"><div class="row row-gap-xs row-align-center"><div class="col col-shrink"><img data-wf--icon--variant="base" src="./welcome_files/CircleCheckYes.svg" alt="" role="presentation" id="" style="" data-component="icon" data-animation-gsap="" data-icon-mode-override="false" class="icon-component"></div><div class="col"><p class="u-mb-0">You are now subscribed.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="col col-lg-7 col-md-12 col-lg-offset-1 col-md-offset-0"><div data-animation-css="fade-4" class="article-text-wrap"><div data-animation-css="small-4" class="u-md-d-block"><div class="w-dyn-list"><div role="list" class="w-dyn-items"><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div><div class="card cc-hoverable"><div class="card-body cc-padding-sm"><p class="paragraph-sm u-text-semibold u-mb-xs">Get started for free</p><p class="paragraph-xs u-mb-sm u-text-pretty">Create custom, scalable websites — without writing code. Start building in Webflow.</p><div><div data-wf--button--variant="text" class="btn w-variant-c1fdf322-f653-7c0b-dcbe-0edb96caab3f"><div aria-hidden="true" class="btn-text">Get started — it's free</div><div class="btn-icon"><div data-wf--button-icon--variant="arrow-right" class="button-icon-wrap"><div class="accordion-line-wrap"><div class="accordion-icon_line cc-horizontal cc-accordion-card"></div><div class="accordion-icon_line cc-vertical cc-accordion-card"></div></div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-right">→</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-up-right">↗</div><div class="button-icon cc-play">►</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-down">↓</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-left">←</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-up">↑</div></div></div></div></div></div><a data-wf-native-id-path="6c4d76eb-ece1-3c7a-138c-13ab50dbeda6_instance-0" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="6c4d76eb-ece1-3c7a-138c-13ab50dbeda6" data-wf-cms-context="%5B%7B%22collectionId%22%3A%226880cdce8157d38adefc593e%22%2C%22itemId%22%3A%226881ec43f7851db0da0ee4b1%22%7D%5D" href="https://webflow.com/signup?utm_source=blog&amp;utm_medium=inline-ad&amp;utm_campaign=signup" class="u-link-overlay w-inline-block"></a></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><p class="subheading-xl u-mb-xl">Need something fresh? Explore these sites if you're searching for a bit of silly fun. Updated for 2025, these picks still hold their quirky charm.</p><div class="article-rich-text w-richtext"><p>Of the many websites making up the internet, only about 18% remain active. Within that minority are the gems — carefully designed yet totally pointless.</p><p>We all need a mindless time-waster to allow our brains to bounce around in the background like old DVD screen savers.</p><p>From labyrinth mazes to trending cursor games, radio time machines, and hacker simulators, If you find yourself needing unexpected amusement, try these whimsical websites. Go on and give these wonderfully random websites a go.</p><div class="w-embed"><ul>
  <li><a href="https://webflow.com/blog/useless-websites#best-useless">Best useless and random sites</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://webflow.com/blog/useless-websites#make-your-own">Make your own random website</a></li>
</ul></div><div class="w-embed"><div id="best-useless"></div></div><h2 id="best-useless-and-random-sites">Best useless and random sites</h2><p>Feel free to share your favorite distraction or discover something new in our curated picks.</p><h3>1. Hacker Typer</h3><figure style="max-width:837pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Hacker Typer website displays a green terminal simulator screen with instructions on how to use the online simulator." src="./welcome_files/68c48c105bf99aefab273a22_660deae74e4d883a78935176_KtzUEHU9X0F1253jhlCeLJLCqxHuEWm07sG1ILNQbdwj0CsW8l1xXhQ_hVkTn0RVHWBvbJ40ncFK499VUxQqBJ7ctlVfGx5cZBrtQSju2a_uWk-_Mnoa_A2us7wiV7bXmdnbmfy-6IvGn2xpJaHdFfs.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>If you’re looking to cosplay like you’re in <em>The Matrix</em>, <a rel="nofollow" href="https://www.hackertyper.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="f3c6cc38-d2d7-fdb6-a933-c8c9c81ffa46" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="f3c6cc38-d2d7-fdb6-a933-c8c9c81ffa46">Hacker Typer</a> is the simulator for you. Upon redirect, you’re presented with a dark screen with green text resembling a command-line interface quintessential to that of ’90s hacker films. And while the website's simply a simulator, it does make for a fun prank or troll.</p><h3>2. Maze Toys</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Bird&#39;s eye view of a digital maze game with endless meandering walls and start and endpoints indicated in red." src="./welcome_files/68c48c115bf99aefab273a38_660deae783ef0ea6c2ccef68_xcOHg9W5rroqQhOhvM7iCRC134sxMEqCAWnurEvu1l5bbY1rw2gp2Rf7yK4cwXnQOAO34pYfto5ykXiBty_QXK6KKQwFGO_M0oVQFd2wK7Eb-kKEhwh5AOZhRC43fpmM0hH9i7sMKp-DzvopvAwErAs.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Be warned, this next one's a true time-killer. Not only is <a rel="nofollow" href="https://maze.toys/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="95420e43-4724-7e1d-b827-01a041f1741e" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="95420e43-4724-7e1d-b827-01a041f1741e">Maze Toys</a> so fun for puzzle fanatics, but it's one of the brainchildren of <a rel="nofollow" href="https://theuselessweb.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="cd5672bd-bf14-60ec-b679-fb1fb79911ad" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="cd5672bd-bf14-60ec-b679-fb1fb79911ad">The Useless Web</a> creator Tim Holland.</p><p>This one's definitely worth checking out. It's fun and interactive, offering three different maze games, Just Maze, Faultless, and Race the Clock, perfect for puzzle lovers looking to pass some time.</p><p>Make sure you have free time; this puzzle can occupy you for quite a while, so pace yourself.</p><h3>3. WindowSwap</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Point of view from a windowsill shows a serene small farm nestled between a wildflower meadow and snow-capped mountain peaks." src="./welcome_files/68c48c115bf99aefab273a4e_660deae789509f283af765ec_CgQ-WFi5n05BFlzmgjg4kxQln0GdNFEQ4QL_GFYzz1_1omzyU9FDURRjI51nkaGakfisbKAX_cALQm8eEeUS2O5BR10wN6Ggnu8eEOJEGayYa6VawFYLgPCrXufo9-lSBJ_e9bF0NVtcpz-R-Uq17OQ.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Ahh, where does one begin with <a rel="nofollow" href="https://www.window-swap.com/Window" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="9fb4434c-07de-98ff-fe83-513b530f0db5" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="9fb4434c-07de-98ff-fe83-513b530f0db5">WindowSwap</a>? Admittedly, it feels like glimpsing someone else's view... But is it, at the same time... satisfying?</p><p>There’s great appeal: real-life video recordings of the POV from windowsills around the world... it’s grounding, connecting. It’s human.</p><p>According to their website, Window Swap is an artist venture where “people from around the world share the view from their windows to help someone else relax, focus, meditate, and travel without moving.”</p><h3>4. Radiooooo</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Interactive world map with iconography, music playback controls, and timestamps from 1900s to 2070 overlaid." src="./welcome_files/68c48c115bf99aefab273a56_660deb4bab40a32dffa2b0ad_EtcfC6ODGFECyPpF0Ya66c9ToDUdIXlQUJrpMR-PnpA31pNBsb-QfcyJN0Uc_CUbXbjXKbG57JijBsvne8HKkBMKciu1D8dxRW5giD3NdDxXh3r1uN2JOQYToC9ErfiJTxq3BU4yL5YxRSl1J8_CkCE.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Ever wondered what was playing on the radio in 1930s Paris? Or perhaps 1970s Taiwan? Well, we've found the perfect time machine for you.</p><p><a rel="nofollow" href="https://radiooooo.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="175eda8a-393e-fcb6-8b49-8394e5429d6f" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="175eda8a-393e-fcb6-8b49-8394e5429d6f">Radiooooo</a> is so, <em>so</em> cool. Simply click the decade and country, and you’ll be transported back in time, listening to the same lost music your grandparents once enjoyed in yesteryear.</p><p>This random website is such a neat concept; a fun, nifty way to come upon “new” old music to add to your playlist.</p><p>It’s available in whatever app store you’re using; give it a download or check out the site.</p><h3>5. Pointer Pointer</h3><p><a rel="nofollow" href="https://pointerpointer.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="ffd939d3-93ad-7fb3-3d22-4f5aca05e214" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="ffd939d3-93ad-7fb3-3d22-4f5aca05e214">Pointer Pointer</a> is quite the random website. Move your cursor across the screen, wait about three seconds, and voilà, a photo of someone, something, or a group of someones will appear on your screen, pointing directly at your cursor.</p><p>Who are these someones? They appear to be friendly faces from the early 2000s. There's something charmingly nostalgic about these snapshots from the sweet, innocent pre-modern-social-media era — a simpler digital time many of us might find ourselves missing today.</p><h3>6. Mondrian and Me</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="One blue, one red and three white squares overlap a canvas, creating an abstract geometric composition." src="./welcome_files/68c48c105bf99aefab273a25_660deb91763a002330b33886_HmcDCkXtuWwnSPd8SBFuBouR6KFZfw9v2UQmadrzin1IzlBxHmWwYL7M4SlZ2w9t4v9t9rwJzboiEh_kDjbmAXUeYHAqG0M-rT-hXL4gXTKVoY3hDPvPM37fbTlbMOzRI2uzsiDDOv2JQMUn_OPBJA8.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Brought to us by the same wonderful mind behind Maze Toys, <a rel="nofollow" href="https://mondrianandme.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="280235e0-5c55-7281-190b-8c6ed73e66f2" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="280235e0-5c55-7281-190b-8c6ed73e66f2">Mondrian and Me</a> is another fun, useless site with an artistic twist. This interactive point-click web page allows you to explore your “artistry” while killing time and indulging in that procrastination itch.</p><h3>7. Bored Button</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="A big red button in the center of the screen labeled &#39;Bored?&#39; invites interaction with a cheeky text description positioned below." src="./welcome_files/68c48c115bf99aefab273a3b_660deb91228187d0d3d616dd_NvhSM7V1vGtuZWPmlQIsNl2RQyt3ZDpGf87rFoDfwqqgeZCsc2SFdBtjwoDRZBzPMRS-_LRG0L7j0pvVqWgViEpJSXXGG2VQPqFf9bHAoUw4DLkasT5276nKmwAfGZFhznQefdJk5FUO57yZ8B3JJTw.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Presenting a big, bright fire truck–red button upon redirect, the <a rel="nofollow" href="https://www.boredbutton.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="bf96a234-ca5a-d8c5-468f-c9fc004ed5ce" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="bf96a234-ca5a-d8c5-468f-c9fc004ed5ce">Bored Button</a> is the only button on the internet here to cure your boredom.</p><p>Just click that big red button and see for yourself. The Bored Button will amuse you with endless fun and quirky internet games, memes, quizzes, and more.</p><h3>8. Always Judge a Book by its Cover</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Website featuring a yellow banner with thick, cursive text &#39;Always Judge a Book by its Cover&#39; and a gag book &#39;How to Talk to Your Cat About Gun Safety&#39; available for purchase." src="./welcome_files/68c48c115bf99aefab273a45_660deb913e16baefa4ecbdc7_f7HB1HBOvFtatXgiiT3StiguYDuX8X1XROEe5A1N1ge-Xv3tfR8MhAeXV6syOR_NvIy-5rQRz_1GA2B03lp2kFwJnNsf8RFMub3qAAPcUUsoyGM3CDlODWKvIMi1iiEYFhd8OtxlaqvWerSOzNYrZoU.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Another brainchild of Tim Holland on our list, except this one isn’t a game, but rather a web page of weird book recommendations, cleverly titled <a rel="nofollow" href="https://alwaysjudgeabookbyitscover.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="5dc7e695-1600-6cea-21e0-f871ce867dfc" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="5dc7e695-1600-6cea-21e0-f871ce867dfc">Always Judge a Book by its Cover</a>.</p><p>The perfect go-to site to find your next gag gift to order online, Always Judge a Book by its Cover houses titles like <em>Toilet Paper Origami</em>, <em>How to Survive a Garden Gnome Attack</em>, and <em>Eating People is Wrong</em>, as well as adult coloring books like <em>Florida Man</em>.</p><p>These definitely are the type of books you’d expect from a website with the tagline, “Some books win awards, some win our hearts and others ... only serve to confuse.” Well said.</p><h3>9. Ffffidget</h3><p>The <a rel="nofollow" href="https://ffffidget.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="ac402ddd-f65b-5a0e-7ef5-eba35db8eb35" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="ac402ddd-f65b-5a0e-7ef5-eba35db8eb35">ffffidget</a> website is the internet’s fidget spinner. Ah, what a magnificently useless website! Add it to the list.</p><p>You click it and it spins, or stops spinning, and so on. If the virtual version doesn’t quite do it for you, don’t be dismayed. You can buy your very own real-life fidget spinner by accessing the hyperlink at the bottom right-hand corner of ffffidget’s web page.</p><h3>10. Try PaP</h3><p>If you’re in need of a silly grin or need to check your password’s strength, look no further than <a rel="nofollow" href="https://trypap.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="648c9b9d-c214-ae4c-7fa0-d6525bbd2a67" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="648c9b9d-c214-ae4c-7fa0-d6525bbd2a67">Try PaP</a>. The brainchild of Tobias van Schneider and Tim Holland, the passive-aggressive password machine, or PaP for short, is <em>not</em> entirely useless.</p><p>A fun gag to test your password’s strength; simply type into the text box and, as Try PaP states, “Imagine your in-laws are helping you with a password ... this is what they’d say.”</p><h3>11. Smash the Walls</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Large neon-pink, hot pink, and yellow triangular shapes with stark, bold black outlines occupy the ends of a bright orange background." src="./welcome_files/68c48c115bf99aefab273a48_660debefa6ccc64b0f7582dc_LdSg3duNQEVFIdRLZJkJUcDfOjk9-tTVJs6yb76bzhiG45NsRhr_VWeW3nnoA37KZqkINLaY_OhrJKU6ScXej3lqCabbQNEDGoT0614AouTKP782FOVhTH4mfaahorUDrzkcNiPTe12HJASJnJMUVz8.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p><a rel="nofollow" href="https://smashthewalls.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="af17a0ee-a7b4-64cd-e606-91179e978c64" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="af17a0ee-a7b4-64cd-e606-91179e978c64">Smash the Walls</a>, or rather, click the colorful walls and watch them crumble to reveal another colorful wall, is another interactive yet incredibly useless website.</p><p>Nevertheless, if you’re into bright, candy-colored, neon graphic web pages that crumble and unveil the next, then have at it. This useless site is for you.</p><h3>12. Weird or Confusing</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Website featuring a pastel purple banner with shrugging emojis and thick, cursive text &#39;Weird or Confusing.&#39; Below the banner is a photorealistic chicken nugget keychain gag gift available for purchase." src="./welcome_files/68c48c115bf99aefab273a4b_660debef94bf60c4c3cea517_XssGbRGtk4vaLcdadY7ola8fdV_MilU0m2PZDKXO_CDxcWrDCiV7bEX5j5vJW0ilK69VcVvIM3uqAW4IgQFHI1qzItS9uyl1CTRE7hNFAsy8RZ_CErO-EV22kSnxCT8OC7pf_V8kp4OIOj1cDXG6yq8.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Looking to buy something weird or confusing beyond the bizarre books mentioned above? Tim Holland has you covered.</p><p>Whether you want to get lost in the depths of the bizarre items available on the internet or need an eccentric gift, <a rel="nofollow" href="http://weirdorconfusing.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="6478d11d-ed31-5bdf-c483-a0f4ef0b499f" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="6478d11d-ed31-5bdf-c483-a0f4ef0b499f">Weird or Confusing</a> is the useless website for this exact niche.</p><h3>13. The Zen Zone</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Gradient pastel blue, purple, and pink logo with black text, &#39;Welcome to The Zen Zone.&#39; Below features descriptive text and a gradient pastel &#39;Let&#39;s get started&#39; button." src="./welcome_files/68c48c115bf99aefab273a35_660debefccc0da67e05e3b80_Jq4Yi7yDdozdgt2AOpXMkYik-xy_Fl7Lvu2hGXrhBaBksFwFwnM_lYulY9j63dgtuFx9vskpCixMaCtryaRHCIuOD93VylZa-6IWc1riufxQbkr1wRu7eyqfPvRccf6GNZRJFxGH4qsGeAdwynx2zK8.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Ah, <a rel="nofollow" href="https://thezen.zone/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="3fc3a114-ba6b-5d5a-4998-6e40e1ab5ab1" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="3fc3a114-ba6b-5d5a-4998-6e40e1ab5ab1">The Zen Zone</a>, another gift from Tim Holland. The Zen Zone is the perfect site to visit for a brief moment of quiet, meditative zen. Hey, not every useless website on the internet has to be absurd.</p><p>No cat GIFs with laser eyes, no doge memes or flashing wacky graphics — none of that. It’s just you and the wholesomely simplistic UI transporting you away to the zenest zones you’ll find online. Choose switch, swirl, or break ... and let the games begin.</p><h3>14. Fish Feeder</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Online game &#39;Fish Feeder&#39; features a blue fish tank with rising bubbles, green swaying seaweed, text instructions, and buttons to select and play a level." src="./welcome_files/68c48c135bf99aefab273acc_660dec4ea2e053bfe9a4d507_brAzsUZeaMwuXeEcHFRYMO17VhWzpVfhE23BVxxhamp6Hg51IHzb8t0_89m0Y4ZonosytH8rPs2gIlvE7jD98mpoud2g9GduUzH5O5hbX_-HI0A9fFzA8R56Ccc5BRQkauW-g1ydxBmMUlgPGLrDZtc.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Creative Tech Guy’s <a rel="nofollow" href="https://creativetechguy.com/fishfeeder" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="4a94cbe9-83dd-d2f9-0f90-c7b1a758ad8a" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="4a94cbe9-83dd-d2f9-0f90-c7b1a758ad8a">Fish Feeder</a> is almost like a love letter to the early internet. Embodying the Microsoft Paint aesthetic of the early 2000s, Fish Feeder is a nostalgia-invoking, time-wasting treat. While not for everyone, if you’re into buying, selling, and breeding fish as you kill time, Jason O’Neill’s got you covered.</p><h3>15. 2048</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Web game 2048 features a beige background with 16 brown-beige square tiles arranged side-by-side on a 4x4 grid with instructions on how to play." src="./welcome_files/68c48c125bf99aefab273ab4_660dec4f07fe64dd89be7f63_BGuGVfpdWdP1L-qzL2qX_G8tIm3J3NeRf1UPIRtEaEsTiZgxvXW6uBaMQPhxzy6lJ-Qd9DUiaA-GnikMoFKnA6CuKctU78rNg8Liv2zZfLelO1UepHFNAiFfwbliILZ63a0bo9LY3JHWo5k46nRYmDM.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>A fun high school throwback if you’re a ’00s child, <a rel="nofollow" href="https://play2048.co/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="29b76281-5170-ce47-99dc-31ae1458238c" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="29b76281-5170-ce47-99dc-31ae1458238c">2048</a> was your sudoku. I, for one, remember being totally terrible at the game but hooked nonetheless.</p><p>As adults, we can't help but enjoy hacking away at the game — burning time as dopamine dances about until that inevitable realization hits:&nbsp;<em>oh yeah, there's work to do</em>.</p><h3>16. Scream into the Void</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Photorealistic blue and black starry sky warps to resemble a swirling black hole with the text &amp;quot;Scream into the Void,&amp;quot;  instructions, and a large red button titled, &#39;SCREAM.&#39;" src="./welcome_files/68c48c135bf99aefab273adf_660dec4f488349077c6e9243_h82CVq0oebxsQnibv3QAr3wiVR3orcQs5wK8W0auDgcQvcu-4bmQ5ard64FmFAo1GOfPenafinkbXJm47ikxbgQW_kDaBrBHSYXed59yC0o0_t5NTVpo_KQ03ExRmLHWL-YK_4c_WJGIzYcXyRDJ73M.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Looking to release a bit of tension? Type out your thoughts with&nbsp;<a rel="nofollow" href="https://screamintothevoid.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="bc3d01e0-4756-824d-496e-e05163b6e5fa" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="bc3d01e0-4756-824d-496e-e05163b6e5fa">Scream into the Void</a>. Type your deepest feelings, frustrations, concerns, or whatever’s got you and scream it into the void ... quite the perfect alternative if you're without paper or a lighter.</p><p><em>But maybe it's not as cathartic?</em></p><h3>17. Neon Flames</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Computer-generated representation of the cosmos highlighted with subtle hues of purple, yellow, red, and white." src="./welcome_files/68c48c135bf99aefab273ad6_660decb808644c1e5a8652b3_Snkh5nvEZ6pnHkwOzIB8mmeBXrT_XzeVgk1PSHJ8LbJBzsWTtx7WThfIPcICebhH3jf1ekD5VEpGkcb4S6pidc9hPWILhQyzzmzdySQLLpfND4hgu4hLNQydAroEWm8N-JqZBcCBjSvhYAxOikYtvi4.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Like The Zen Zone, <a rel="nofollow" href="https://29a.ch/sandbox/2011/neonflames/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="db560095-c65a-50a3-37b1-262b4b6b049a" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="db560095-c65a-50a3-37b1-262b4b6b049a">Neon Flames</a> can be described as a meditative zen. Brought to us by Jonas Wagner’s <a rel="nofollow" href="https://29a.ch/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="ae163208-1b7d-62b5-7a20-37152dcfc71b" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="ae163208-1b7d-62b5-7a20-37152dcfc71b">29a.ch</a>, this “paint your own nebula” web page is so cool.</p><p>Simply choose a color and drag your cursor across the cosmos, painting your very own nebula as you go along. The longer you hold your cursor, the brighter the color;&nbsp; just a fun FYI.</p><h3>18. Patience Is a Virtue</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="White loading screen displays gray text &#39;Loading, please wait&#39; and a small, circular blue loading graphic." src="./welcome_files/68c48c135bf99aefab273ac1_660decb874987f6d737efa40_G9VB-h5iYRepPXA8MiteobnuT2KLclWdFTXAzkjtCpfqIJCtgecepIk4i0y5YDLtH2AYowmCMaHAI5LJtyk_IAY_2qnl8rdHVKSIsaXXl9Yc3XdT5wMZqdVynSq9mo-QCmtzzcWtvM5A-zn6d0f4Xaw.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p><a rel="nofollow" href="http://www.patience-is-a-virtue.org/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="1bc37d33-c2e8-349d-70d6-26b7971b8eac" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="1bc37d33-c2e8-349d-70d6-26b7971b8eac">Patience Is a Virtue</a> is a wonderfully flippant web page, perfect for your next troll or April Fools’ Day. What is this magnificent beauty? A blank, loading web page.</p><p>Yes, a blank, forever-loading web page. To what?</p><p>Perhaps we’ll never know.</p><h3>19. Endless Horse</h3><figure style="max-width:1600pxpx" class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="A white screen displays a rudimentary key-stroke illustration of a horse with endless legs." src="./welcome_files/68c48c125bf99aefab273ab1_660decb8ccc0da67e05f2e4b_Ytx3bFZY9rhWOrimnvExHAksHG-9d_GLO7yZnfyiMTwYBMnVrDgmJvRgoLlqi_5wX2yEzSayoC0hRIRvizXu2lgz5CfkatWpaEqiUsD4SvPxCK78PbF2i3jTUqW_8w89EZ1v-vrzeYsPXP1NKkBF59g.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p><a rel="nofollow" href="http://endless.horse/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="eb59274b-7284-5c1b-d8f3-c815c6f2e028" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="eb59274b-7284-5c1b-d8f3-c815c6f2e028">Endless Horse</a>; the lovely, lackluster cousin to the once-trending Long Doge Challenge.</p><p>While there are no “wows” or cute doge dogs, there is a pixel horse. And you’ve guessed correctly, the horse gets long. The URL speaks for itself: It’s the endless horse. <em>What else would you expect from such a useless website?</em></p><h3>20. Paper Toilet</h3><figure class="w-richtext-align-center w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img alt="Paper Toilet website displays a large, white toilet paper roll on a black background." src="./welcome_files/68c48c125bf99aefab273ab7_660decb8f0193af19ad60320_heGtTAMjIJGchVywsB0wJ2Pa9ELGM4auw883AEi2TXQ6Snr0Yh99GQoqVPaMTIkaWsl1hjlMrMvD7ulUNhHG172ICy7q0X44Phbz88Usok-ru2NdQ5nE05pQoVylrLCE-oIuhuD138_ewsBCKlR8ZgY.png" loading="lazy"></div></figure><p>Topping off our list is perhaps the most useless website, <a rel="nofollow" href="https://papertoilet.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="934fe617-a28f-35ae-5ee2-b8b0a619645f" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="934fe617-a28f-35ae-5ee2-b8b0a619645f">Paper Toilet</a>. Not to be confused with toilet paper. Paper Toilet is a web page featuring a single toilet paper roll on a black screen. Scroll, and the rest is weird internet history.</p><div class="w-embed"><div id="make-your-own"></div></div><h2 id="make-your-own-random-website">Make your own random website</h2><p>So that’s our list; 20 of the best, most useless websites you can find online. And for those feeling extra inspired, design your own weird, random, “useless” website with <a href="https://webflow.com/" data-wf-native-id-path="1c5bc5bf-2c87-457c-a5f0-1c93a9b6ea7f" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="1c5bc5bf-2c87-457c-a5f0-1c93a9b6ea7f">Webflow</a>.</p><p>From there, get eyes on your creation by submitting to <a rel="nofollow" href="https://theuselessweb.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="38eecdb2-6c39-3672-2aed-83229a41f7fa" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="38eecdb2-6c39-3672-2aed-83229a41f7fa">The Useless Web</a> or&nbsp;<a rel="nofollow" href="https://www.bestuselesswebsites.com/" target="_blank" data-wf-native-id-path="671a1e6b-2e06-8648-1c81-4fdbac8ec260" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="671a1e6b-2e06-8648-1c81-4fdbac8ec260">Best Most Useless Websites</a> — both platforms are currently accepting new&nbsp;entries.</p></div></div><div><div><div class="card cc-border-none"><div class="card-body u-bg-secondary u-radius-base"><div class="row"><div class="col"><p class="subheading">Get started for free</p><p class="paragraph-sm u-text-secondary">Create custom, scalable websites — without writing code. Start building in Webflow.</p><div><div data-wf--button--variant="text" class="btn w-variant-c1fdf322-f653-7c0b-dcbe-0edb96caab3f"><div aria-hidden="true" class="btn-text">Unleash your creativity on the web</div><div class="btn-icon"><div data-wf--button-icon--variant="arrow-right" class="button-icon-wrap"><div class="accordion-line-wrap"><div class="accordion-icon_line cc-horizontal cc-accordion-card"></div><div class="accordion-icon_line cc-vertical cc-accordion-card"></div></div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-right">→</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-up-right">↗</div><div class="button-icon cc-play">►</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-down">↓</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-left">←</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-up">↑</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><a data-cta-text="Get started for free" data-cta="20 best useless websites to visit when you’re bored" data-cta-position="Final Ad" data-wf-native-id-path="5c51f7fe-821d-0d00-8b97-62c4cb90621a" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="5c51f7fe-821d-0d00-8b97-62c4cb90621a" href="https://webflow.com/signup?utm_source=blog&amp;utm_medium=inline-ad&amp;utm_campaign=signup" class="u-link-cover w-inline-block"><div class="u-sr-only">Read now</div></a></div></div></div><hr data-wf--border--spacing="none" class="u-border"><div class="row"><div class="col col-lg-6"><div data-wf--eyebrow--alignment="left" class="eyebrow-component"><div class="eyebrow caption">Last Updated</div></div><div>February 27, 2026</div></div><div class="col col-lg-6"><div data-wf--eyebrow--alignment="left" class="eyebrow-component"><div class="eyebrow caption">Category</div></div><div class="u-d-inline-block"><div class="w-embed"><a href="https://webflow.com/blog/category/design">Design</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><hr data-wf--border--spacing="none" class="u-border"><section class="section"><div class="container"><div data-slider="component" class="slider_wrap" data-script-initialized="true"><div class="row row-align-end row-justify-between"><div class="col col-shrink"><div data-wf--heading--alignment="left-align" class="heading-component"><h2 class="u-mb-0">Related articles</h2></div></div><div class="col col-shrink"><div data-wf--grid---row--column-alignment="center-right" row-gap-xs="" class="row-component"><div class="row w-variant-84c0d3ac-e67c-aa17-8572-49b2e539ff14 row-gap-xs"><div data-wf--grid---column--column-size="shrink" class="col w-variant-63569d8e-a8ac-61e1-0666-21eb6073c541"><div class="slot cc-column"><button data-wf--circle-button--button-type="base" id="" data-slider="previous" aria-label="Previous slide" class="circle-btn swiper-button-disabled" disabled="" tabindex="-1" aria-controls="swiper-wrapper-58ac310f15c836a37" aria-disabled="true"><div data-wf--button-icon--variant="arrow-left" class="button-icon-wrap"><div class="accordion-line-wrap"><div class="accordion-icon_line cc-horizontal cc-accordion-card"></div><div class="accordion-icon_line cc-vertical cc-accordion-card"></div></div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-right w-variant-e8e20059-6a8d-8967-e1ec-eb97ad70de3f">→</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-up-right">↗</div><div class="button-icon cc-play">►</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-down">↓</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-left w-variant-e8e20059-6a8d-8967-e1ec-eb97ad70de3f">←</div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-up">↑</div></div></button></div></div><div data-wf--grid---column--column-size="shrink" class="col w-variant-63569d8e-a8ac-61e1-0666-21eb6073c541"><div class="slot cc-column"><button data-wf--circle-button--button-type="base" id="" data-slider="next" aria-label="Next slide" class="circle-btn" tabindex="0" aria-controls="swiper-wrapper-58ac310f15c836a37" aria-disabled="false"><div data-wf--button-icon--variant="arrow-right" class="button-icon-wrap"><div class="accordion-line-wrap"><div class="accordion-icon_line cc-horizontal cc-accordion-card"></div><div class="accordion-icon_line cc-vertical cc-accordion-card"></div></div><div class="button-icon cc-arrow-right">→</div><div class="button-